<article class="env-corollary" id="E3F0F5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/E3F0F5">Corollary <span data-tag="E3F0F5">3.1.4.3</span>.</a> Let $f: A \rightarrow B$ be a cofibration in $(\mSet )_{/S}$ and $f': A' \rightarrow B'$ a cofibration in $(\mSet )_{/T}$. Then the smash product map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[ (A \times B' ) \coprod _{ A \times B } (A' \times B) \rightarrow A' \times B' \]
</div>
  <p> is a cofibration in $(\mSet )_{/S \times T}$, which is trivial if either $f$ or $g$ is trivial. </p>
</article>